{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And Elohim created the man in His image.</b> With the die prepared for him — for all was created by utterance, but he was created by hand, as it says ״וַתָּשֶׁת עָלַי כַּפֶּכָה״ (Psalms 139). He was made with a seal, like a coin stamped by an impression called קוי״ן בְּלַעַ״ז, and thus it says ״תִּתְהַפֵּךְ כְּחֹמֶר חוֹתָם״ (Job 38)." "<b>In the image of Elohim He created him.</b> He explains to you that that image prepared for him is the form of the likeness of his Maker." "<b>Male and female He created them.</b> But further on it says ״וַיִּקַּח אַחַת מִצַּלְעֹתָיו ״ (Genesis 2)? This is its midrash — that He created him with two faces in the first creation, and afterward divided him. And the plain sense of Scripture: here He informs you that both were created on the sixth day and did not spell out for you how they were created; He spelled that out for you elsewhere."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French coigne, 'die/mint-stamp'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:13.178995057Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}